 "title": "How to make anyone like you",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video discusses how to build charisma by making people feel liked and valued. The creator explains that people are drawn to those who clearly signal warmth and openness.",
 "key_points": [
  "People like those who clearly signal warmth and liking, rather than being mute or undersignaling.",
  "Use phrases like 'It's so fun talking to you', 'You always have the best stories', or 'I love when you're put on my team'.",
  "82% of impressions of people are based on warmth and competence.",
  "First, people signal 'I'm open, I'm friendly' (warmth).",
  "Second, people signal 'I'm capable, efficient, effective' (competence).",
  "Every human being you first meet is trying to answer two questions: Can I trust you? Can I rely on you?"
 ],
 "content": "DOAC Vanessa Van Edwards. HOW TO MAKE ANYONE LIKE YOU. Charisma Expert. If you are trying to teach me to have aura and rizz, what are like the basics? It's someone that you really want to be around. It's when they walk into a room, you want to go over and talk to them, you want to sit near them, you want to listen to them, you want to work with them. We like to be around people who are one, clearly signaling. We don't like people who are mute with their body language, we don't like people who undersignal. We like people who clearly like us. So saying things like, it's always so fun talking to you or oh, you always have the best stories. Oh, you always make me laugh. I love when you're put on my team. We so want to be liked that when someone clearly signals liking, it makes us like them more. Fundamentally, 82% of our impressions of people are based on warmth and competence. So people who are first signaling I'm open, I'm friendly, and then competent, I'm capable, I'm efficient, I'm effective, make us feel like I'm in good hands. In this way, every human being we first meet, we're trying to answer two questions: Can I trust you and can I rely on you? The second thing that charismatic people are doing is they're signaling you can trust me and you can rely on me. I'm going to get it done, I'm going to only speak when I know something, I'm going to be assertive, I'm going to carry us through this conversation. And so I think that that plan is a secret door into charisma. Text shown on screen: DOAC, Vanessa Van Edwards, Charisma Expert, HOW TO MAKE ANYONE LIKE YOU.",
